{"chunk_id": "e13f2c5b9793", "text": "Tara warns Bali not to answer Sugriva\u2019s challenge, fearing danger from Rama, but the proud monkey king refuses to endure the insult of combat avoidance. Confident that the righteous Rama would never strike unfairly, Bali reassures her and marches out, vowing only to humble his brother rather than kill him. After a sorrowful farewell in which Tara ritually circles him and returns to the palace in tears, Bali storms from the city in fury. He soon confronts Sugriva, and the brothers clash in a ferocious duel. They hurl trees, strike with fists, knees, and feet, and fight like titanic forces of nature. Though valiant, Sugriva begins to falter and signals to Rama for aid, setting the stage for Bali\u2019s fateful wound.\nIgnoring Tara\u2019s warning, Bali confronts Sugriva in a furious duel while Rama watches, waiting for the moment to strike.\nThemes: brotherly rivalry, warrior honor, foreboding warning, duel, fate and hubris", "vector": [-0.004672082141041756, -0.04685663804411888, 0.0029658894054591656, -0.005792567040771246, 0.008495312184095383, 0.017927756533026695, -0.019150104373693466, -0.010023245587944984, -0.03392692282795906, -0.024881552904844284, -0.0012698827777057886, 0.002380181336775422, 0.023183848708868027, 0.00041126884752884507, 0.007619296666234732, 0.00033423551940359175, 0.04835061728954315, -0.009418862871825695, 0.017914175987243652, -0.005595633294433355, -0.01091284304857254, 0.007320500444620848, -0.0032069634180516005, 0.007693995721638203, -0.01878339983522892, 0.015265756286680698, 0.015157103538513184, -0.034443024545907974, 0.003999791108071804, -0.016705410555005074, -0.011279546655714512, -0.012264215387403965, 0.0035244340542703867, 0.0013428840320557356, -0.025003787130117416, -0.007531016133725643, 2.0611190848285332e-05, 0.0010568208526819944, 0.004661895800381899, -0.004451380576938391, -0.0023496225476264954, 0.008773735724389553, -0.001811450463719666, -0.008848434314131737, -0.008278